{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pass-1 test-sufficiency review of the diff touching `tests/test_reducer.py`:\n\n- [ ] `test_apply_event` is a tautological assertion: `m = Mock(return_value=42); assert m() == 42` verifies only the `unittest.mock` framework's configured return, not the reducer. The named unit (`apply_event`) is never invoked, so the test has zero regression coverage of any reducer behavior — it would pass regardless of any change to the code it purports to cover. Replace with a test that calls the real `apply_event` and asserts on its observable output. (The `monkeypatch` fixture is also requested but unused.)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785712933666226001,"uuid":"d833d9f7-4377-4772-9b54-e35209458a59"}